The addition of `kfree(hostcmd);` in the error handling path ensures that if `mwifiex_send_cmd` fails, the allocated memory for `hostcmd` is properly freed, preventing the memory leak. Similar additions are made for other error paths to ensure that `hostcmd` is always freed when an error occurs.


